nsumed by routing, footer/state logic, DevPad/server surfaces, and Cable Car contract tests. `MODEL != SEAT` is mechanically enforced: model tokens, retired seats, and HOLD seats fail routing rather than silently forwarding. fileciteturn0file0L35-L40\n\nThe main failure is therefore **not architecture**.\n\nIt is **state convergence**.\n\nFour classes of drift remain:\n\n1. **Current machine canon vs stale prose canon.**\n2. **Current seat roster vs stale bootstrap language.**\n3. **Seat-based routing vs still-live model-address transport.**\n4. **Identity directories as control surfaces vs bootstrap instructions that still encourage working inside them.**\n\nLuce also verified that the prior competing-bootstrap problem and the DevPad identity-cwd launch mechanism have already been corrected. fileciteturn0file0L78-L94\n\n### CODA RECONCILIATION\n\n**The machine substrate survives.**\n\nWe are not rebuilding routing.\n\nWe are aligning the surrounding control surfaces to it.\n\n---\n\n# 2. FROZEN ROSTER VS DISK\n\n## Current frozen roster\n\n**ACTIVE / CURRENT**\n\nDon  \nCoda  \nVittorio  \nChiave  \nNico  \nCorrado  \nFalcon  \nTalon  \nKeel  \nLuce  \nMagpie  \nPigeon  \nRaven\n\n**RETIRED**\n\nRagno  \nKimi  \nCalibro\n\n**HOLD / NOT SEATS IN ACTIVE USE**\n\nGLM  \nKimi_Plumb\n\nSpace Bunny and Big Pickle remain **occupants/models**, not seats.\n\n### Disk discrepancy\n\nThe registry still represents **Ragno as loadable/on-demand**, while the current Don ruling explicitly retires Ragno. Luce correctly stopped instead of choosing between those authorities. fileciteturn0file0L98-L100\n\n### CODA RULING\n\n**The current Don ruling governs. Ragno is RETIRED.**\n\nTherefore the registry is **technically current but semantically one revision behind** until Nico performs the atomic Ragno retirement update.\n\nThis is no longer an unresolved decision.\n\n---\n\n# 3. CANON / AUTHORITY MAP\n\n| Surface | Classification | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|\n| `seat_registry.json` | **CURRENT MACHINE AUTHORITY** | KEEP + update Ragno |\n| `GCE_SEAT_ROUTER.md` | **CURRENT MACHINE-ALIGNED PROSE ROUTER** | KEEP + update Ragno |\n| routing state / footer / registry JS | **CURRENT EXECUTION AUTHORITY** | KEEP |\n| storage taxonomy freeze | **CURRENT POLICY** | KEEP |\n| universal bootstrap schema | **CURRENT STRUCTURE, PARTIALLY STALE CONTENT** | KEEP + surgical correction |\n| `GCE_ORG\\README.md` | **STALE PROSE CANON** | SUPERSEDE |\n| `02_COUNCILS\\README-CANONICAL.md` | **STALE PROSE CANON** | SUPERSEDE |\n| old technical-strategy manifest | **STALE** | SUPERSEDE |\n| old EdgeCrew methodology README | **STALE** | SUPERSEDE |\n| `GCE_DON\\AGENTS.md` | **STALE LIVE BOOTSTRAP-LIKE SURFACE** | NEUTRALIZE |\n| Mailroom `seats.json` | **DORMANT SUBSYSTEM COPY** | LEAVE FOR LATER |\n\nLuce found four independently represented roster surfaces and, critically, the 2026-09-02 prose canon still calls itself canonical while naming Kimi and Big Pickle as identities. fileciteturn0file0L149-L177\n\n### CODA RULING — D-2\n\n**The registry is the singular roster/machine authority.**\n\nHuman-readable GCE_ORG roster documents are **derived explanatory surfaces**, not independent canon.\n\nTherefore:\n\n> **Do not rewrite a second authoritative org chart.**\n\nBanner the obsolete September 2 documents **SUPERSEDED**, retain them as provenance, and point readers to:\n\n1. `seat_registry.json`\n2. `GCE_SEAT_ROUTER.md`\n3. the current Framework anchor/session authority where appropriate.\n\nThis removes dual canon instead of maintaining two supposedly canonical copies.\n\n---\n\n# 4. LIVE BOOTSTRAP AUDIT\n\nThe bootstrap mechanism itself is healthy:\n\n- 13 loadable bootstraps.\n- zero deny-list violations.\n- no rogue `AGENTS.md` within GCE_ORG.\n- both previously discovered competing bootstraps are bannered/neutralized.\n- routing no longer resolves seat identities through model names. fileciteturn0file0L203-L219\n\nThe remaining defect is *