ed handoff creation from Coda into that transport.\n\nThat is the distinction Nico just forced us to see.\n\n---\n\n# The actual defect\n\nCall it something like:\n\n**CABLE CAR REMOTE PRODUCER GAP**\n\nor more specifically:\n\n**Coda → Cable Car ingress adapter missing**\n\nCoda needs a supported operation equivalent to:\n\n```text\nemit_handoff(\n    from=Coda,\n    to=Nico,\n    project=FRAMEWORK,\n    payload=...\n)\n```\n\nAnd that operation must do all of this atomically:\n\n1. Build the envelope using the **actual Cable Car contract**.\n2. Validate it **before delivery**.\n3. Generate the canonical filename from `handoff_id`.\n4. Write the raw JSON to the actual Drive `01_INBOUND_TO_GCE`.\n5. Read it back / confirm Drive ID.\n6. Report **DELIVERED**, not merely **CREATED**.\n7. Only then tell Nico to run intake.\n\nThat is the missing capability.\n\n## We also discovered a second defect\n\nRight now I can apparently compose an envelope that *looks* reasonable but may not satisfy the repo validator.\n\nNico specifically caught the earlier test artifact carrying things like:\n\n```text\nrequested_destination: \"Nico\"\nproject: \"GCE_Stack/Cable_Car\"\n```\n\nwhile the newer contract expects richer routing semantics and has project-pattern constraints.\n\nSo Coda **should not hand-author JSON from memory**.\n\nThe remote producer needs to use the **same canonical contract implementation/validator as Cable Car**.\n\nIdeally:\n\n```text\nCoda intent\n   ↓\ncanonical handoff builder\n   ↓\nvalidate-envelope\n   ↓\nDrive ingress\n   ↓\nCable Car\n```\n\nNot:\n\n```text\nCoda guesses JSON\n   ↓\nDrive\n   ↓\n98_QUARANTINE\n```\n\n---\n\n# What I would hand Nico separately\n\nThe inline Framework package you are sending him is still fine for getting today's work moving.\n\nBut **this transport defect is a separate Framework implementation item** and should be parked rather than contaminating Nico's taxonomy pass:\n\n> **Build a first-class remote producer/ingress ada