e DevPad** as a separate ad hoc / backup / model-audition surface.\n\n### Purpose\n\nRookie is for:\n\n- ad hoc work\n- experiments\n- scratch sessions\n- temporary model auditions\n- overflow\n- quick one-off jobs\n- backup capacity\n\nIt must **not** replace or modify the Main DevPad.\n\n### Doctrine\n\n- `MODEL != SEAT`\n- seat identities remain stable\n- model/runtime occupants are swappable\n- Rookie is not a permanent B-team roster\n- no Rookie state may contaminate Main DevPad state\n- use the same seat/router doctrine as Main\n- keep its state/session/route surface separate and clearly marked `ROOKIE / AD HOC`\n\n### First-pass Rookie occupant pool\n\nUse these as the initial audition candidates, not permanent bindings:\n\n- Coda → Nex N2.5 Pro\n- Chiave → Nex N2.5 Pro\n- Vittorio → Dots3 Note Preview\n- Nico → Space Bunny or MiMo V2.6 Flash\n- Luce → Big Pickle or Nex Mini\n- Talon → Muse Spark 1.3\n- Keel → Space Bunny / MiMo / Nex depending build task\n- Falcon → Ling 3.0 Flash Fin\n- Corrado → only load when real quant work exists; choose model by task\n- keep GLM 5.1, Kimi K3, Qwen, Meumtron and other free/cheap models available in the audition pool\n\n### Important findings to preserve\n\n- Big Pickle stays in the pool; do not blacklist it based on one bad task.\n- GLM was excellent on structured/data correction work where other models struggled.\n- Space Bunny performed strongly in Nico-style implementation.\n- MiMo can work but has gotten stuck; treat as replaceable.\n- Kimi heavy/stateful behavior can vary by runtime/model mode.\n- provider/rate-limit reliability matters separately from cognitive quality.\n\n### Build requirement\n\nClone only the **board mechanics and seat routing behavior** needed for Rookie.\n\nDo not clone Main state.\n\nCreate a separate Rookie config/state namespace and obvious visual label.\n\nMake swapping a model occupant for a seat easy and reversible.\n\nDo not redesign the Main DevPad, Cable Car, routing architecture, or