ng, Transport/Cable Car, VoiceBridge, etc. fileciteturn23file0L103-L119\n\n---\n\n## Structure I would freeze\n\nReuse the existing project doctrine rather than invent another one:\n\n```text\nGCE/\n└── 03_PROJECTS/\n    └── GCE_Stack/\n        └── Rookie_DevPad/\n            ├── 00_CURRENT/\n            │   ├── ROOKIE_ENVIRONMENT_DOCTRINE.md\n            │   ├── ROOKIE_ROSTER_CURRENT.md\n            │   └── ROOKIE_BOOTSTRAP_MANIFEST.md\n            │\n            ├── 01_HANDOFFS/\n            │   ├── Coda/\n            │   ├── Vittorio/\n            │   ├── Chiave/\n            │   ├── Nico/\n            │   ├── Corrado/\n            │   ├── Falcon/\n            │   ├── Talon/\n            │   ├── Keel/\n            │   ├── Luce/\n            │   ├── Magpie/\n            │   ├── Pigeon/\n            │   └── Raven/\n            │\n            ├── 02_WORK/\n            │\n            ├── 03_REGISTRY/\n            │   ├── ROOKIE_IDENTITY_REGISTER.md\n            │   ├── ROOKIE_OCCUPANT_REGISTER.md\n            │   └── ROOKIE_SUPERSESSION_REGISTER.md\n            │\n            ├── 04_DECISIONS/\n            │\n            ├── Identities/\n            │   ├── Coda/\n            │   ├── Vittorio/\n            │   ├── Chiave/\n            │   ├── Nico/\n            │   ├── Corrado/\n            │   ├── Falcon/\n            │   ├── Talon/\n            │   ├── Keel/\n            │   ├── Luce/\n            │   ├── Magpie/\n            │   ├── Pigeon/\n            │   └── Raven/\n            │\n            └── 90_HISTORICAL/\n```\n\nThe `00_CURRENT / 01_HANDOFFS / 02_WORK / 03_REGISTRY / 04_DECISIONS / 90_HISTORICAL` pattern is already reused across the live Drive project structure, so this is copying established doctrine rather than adding another taxonomy. fileciteturn23file0L103-L120\n\n---\n\n## D4 — Rookie identity naming\n\nI agree with Luce's proposed separation:\n\n> **Folder key = canonical seat.**  \n> **Rookie identity = metadata inside the folder.**  \n> **Model occupant = dynamic runtime state.**\n\nSo:\n\n```text\nIdentities/Nico/\n    ROOKIE_IDENTITY.md\n    BOOTSTRAP_ROOKIE.md\n    OCCUPANT_STATE.md\n```\n\nmight contain:\n\n```text\nCanonical seat: Nico\nRookie identity: Ferro\nCurrent occupant: Nex N2.5 Pro\n```\n\nBut we **do not** make:\n\n```text\nIdentities/Ferro/\n```\n\nthe routing authority.\n\nThat keeps:\n\n**SEAT != ROOKIE IDENTITY != MODEL**\n\nmechanically obvious.\n\nThe recon specifically found that the existing Rookie draft set already uses 12 overlay identities — Notaio, Sable, Muro, Ferro, Abaco, Falco, Volo, Chiglia, Specchio, Archivio, Rondine, and Calamaio — and that the intended doctrine is an overlay on canonical seats with models remaining dynamic. fileciteturn23file0L66-L79\n\n---\n\n## Remaining decisions\n\nI would resolve the rest without contaminating this build:\n\n**D3 Ragno:** preserve the residual folders but mark **RETIRED / DO NOT LOAD**. Don't delete provenance.\n\n**D5 empty folders:** leave them alone. No mass pruning in Rookie build.\n\n**D6 loose handoffs / duplicates:** separate cleanup. Do not move them during Rookie implementation.\n\n**D7 empty Framework anchor:** real defect, but fix in Framework current-state work, not Rookie structure.\n\n**D8 Talon shared-state coupling:** definitely separate. It is load-bearing cross-seat infrastructure and should not be casually moved.\n\nLuce also found the local seat source pattern we should copy conceptually: `AGENTS.md + SESSION_HEADER.md + <SEAT>_CONTRACT.md + <SEAT>_LOAD_ROOT.md`, while explicitly avoiding work product, nested competing bootstraps, and identity-home pollution. fileciteturn23file0L153-L172\n\n## So the build doctrine is now simple\n\n**Do not duplicate `GCE_IDENTITY`.**\n\nCanonical seat identity remains where it is.\n\nRookie creates an **overlay identity/bootstrap package inside `GCE_Stack/Rookie_DevPad`** that points back to canonical seat authority and carries only Rookie-specific identity, runt