ied\n- content hash verified\n- no active retry/recovery dependency\n- no identity ambiguity\n- not durable 06_HANDOFFS evidence\n- not retired/model-lane provenance\n- not otherwise held by explicit policy\n\nOtherwise HOLD.\n\nDo not use age alone.\n\n## 5. SEAT/BOOTSTRAP BEHAVIOR\n\nUpdate shared bootstrap/runtime doctrine so every seat knows:\n\n- approved Drive access path\n- how to test it\n- when to STOP\n- what evidence qualifies as “Drive unavailable”\n- never invent local mirrors\n- never substitute local FS for Drive\n- destination seat is routing, not ownership transfer\n- Drive access behavior is framework doctrine, not seat-specific tribal knowledge\n\n# CLEANUP FINDINGS TO ADDRESS\n\n## F-4 — Ragno archive path mismatch\n\nRegistry references:\n\n`GCE_ARCHIVE\\2026-09-25_GCE_seat_retirement_Ragno`\n\nbut path does not exist.\n\nPreserve the sole surviving Ragno evidence.\n\nImplement a safe, hash-verified retirement archive reference/path correction without deleting provenance.\n\n## F-5 — native Google Doc in inbound\n\nCanonical transport envelope remains JSON.\n\nUnsupported payload must become loud and typed:\n\n`UNSUPPORTED_PAYLOAD_TYPE`\n\nDo not silently parse native docs as valid handoffs.\n\n## F-6 — Drive/local identity disagreement\n\nOne Drive ID currently serves two handoff IDs.\n\nHarden identity correlation and fail closed on conflict.\n\nAdd regression coverage.\n\n## F-7 — historical contract violations\n\nDo not rewrite the 11 existing historical violations.\n\nNo increase allowed.\n\n## F-8 — `_shared` mixed content\n\nAdd typed discrimination between:\n\n- inbox message\n- transport envelope\n\nDo not infer type from filename alone.\n\n## F-9 — ledger source_ref volatility\n\nA local outbox path must not be the only durable identity of a transfer.\n\nRetain backward compatibility, but persist enough durable identity to trace:\n\nlocal staging\n→ handoff_id\n→ Drive file ID\n→ content hash\n→ terminal ledger state\n\n## F-10 — stale