tructure — but the screenshot alone doesn't prove which.\n\nRun this in PowerShell:\n\n```powershell\nGet-CimInstance Win32_Process |\n  Where-Object { $_.Name -like \"bun*\" } |\n  Select-Object ProcessId, ParentProcessId, CommandLine |\n  Format-List\n```\n\nThat will tell us exactly **which Bun command owns each ~1.1 GB process**.\n\nIf one is Main and one is Rookie, **beautiful — that's the separation we want**.\n\nIf they're both pointing at the same DevPad/server command, then we just found a duplicate-runtime/leak problem worth fixing.", "text_chars": 1112, "code_blocks": 1, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "ca51b15d-2726-45cb-aaa2-c986fd159202", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790400053.075, "updated_at": 1790400062.500007, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "nnbothing happened", "text_chars": 18, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "a5afefb2-f714-45bd-a9bd-d00c83d1de58", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790400057.233754, "updated_at": 1790400075.031542, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "If that command returned nothing, PowerShell probably isn’t seeing the executable name as `bun*`.\n\nUse this broader one:\n\n```powershell\nGet-CimInstance Win32_Process |\n  Where-Object { $_.CommandLine -match \"bun|devpad|rookie|voice\" } |\n  Select-Object Name, ProcessId, ParentProcessId, CommandLine |\n  Format-List\n```\n\nThat searches the **command line**, not just the process name.\n\nIf that still returns nothing, use:\n\n```powershell\nGet-Pro