: 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "f9ce729c-9319-49ac-bc79-31a7d47e4931", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790401049.5960932, "updated_at": 1790401067.047353, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Please tell me you ensured that what we're doing is basically ripping out where it loads and putting it in the right place with everything. It's gonna not break the reference, correct?", "text_chars": 184, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "1165cc82-da87-4094-aed6-d45ef33f9474", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790401052.99176, "updated_at": 1790401052.99176, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "753e9cb5-3239-4ffc-abfd-369fb4930524", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790401054.426856, "updated_at": 1790401054.426856, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "8e0939ed-64ef-4759-9b25-494815fd62d0", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790401054.429574, "updated_at": 1790401066.619525, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes — that is the intent.\n\nWe are **not deleting the capability**. We are removing it from the **wrong global startup surface** and preserving/re-pointing it so it loads **only from the correct project/provider context**.\n\nSo the safe pattern is:\n\n```text\nCURRENT BAD STATE\n\nPowerShell / profile root\n    ↓\nauto-loads Kimi / GLM / stale project instructions\n    ↓\ngeneric OpenCode session inherits them\n```\n\nbecomes:\n\n```text\nTARGET STATE\n\nNeutral PowerShell / neutral profile root\n    ↓\nselect active project / provider\n    ↓\nload that project/provider's own config\n    ↓\nOpenCode starts from correct runtime root\n```\n\nThe prompt explicitly tells Nico to:\n\n- **back up before modifying**\n- **not delete provider installations**\n- **preserve explicit provider launch capability**\n- **remove stale project-specific instructions from the neutral root**\n- **move/relocate live project logic to the project where it belongs**\n- **reconcile router/registry references**\n- **not delete historical project data**\n- **verify healthy current sessions and routing remain intact**\n\nSo, for example, if the WNBA Tracker content is still a real project artifact, the correct action is **remove it from profile-root startup and put/keep it in the WNBA project surface**, then ensure any active references point there.\n\nSame for Kimi/GLM:\n\n- binaries/config stay installed\n- global auto-load goes away\n- explicit launch still works\n- PATH/bootstrap references are corrected so nothing points at a dead location\n\nThe one thing I would add to Nico’s acceptance criteria to make this airtight is:\n\n> **For every item removed from profile-root startup, prove its surviving canonical destination or explicit retirement status, and verify all live references resolve after the move. No dangling references allowed.**\n\nThat is the exact safeguard against “cleaning it up” and accidentally breaking the framework.", "text_chars": 1890, "code_blocks": 2, "links": [], "citati