l", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 1, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "b266c326-f5e4-4a89-b780-0503ec2843b8", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790402226.084659, "updated_at": 1790402226.084659, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "8fcf41f5-a6b9-435b-810d-77b8e27cc573", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790402226.088149, "updated_at": 1790402226.088149, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "1b38035d-c384-4858-986e-870c000aee03", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790402226.092499, "updated_at": 1790402259.448197, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yep — I just re-read the **current Google Drive session-control family**, and you’re remembering it correctly. We already built most of this. The new insight tonight is that **Hypothesis needs to become first-class**, because right now Intent + Objective are explicit but hypothesis is mostly implicit.\n\n## What exists now\n\nThe parent is:\n\n**`GCE_SESSION_FRAME_V3_CURRENT_2026-09-25`**\n\nIts hierarchy is already:\n\n```text\nSESSION FRAME V3\n│\n├── Header\n│   ├── Don Intent Snapshot\n│   └── Active Context Board\n│\n├── Mid-Flight Frame\n│\n├── Checkpoint Frame\n│\n└── Footer\n    └── Routing / Handoff Appendix\n```\n\nAnd underneath that we now have class-specific controls:\n\n```text\nExecutive Council\n├── SESSION HEADER V1\n└── SESSION FOOTER V1\n\nShared Services\n├── SESSION HEADER V1\n└── SESSION FOOTER V1\n```\n\nplus the normalized:\n\n**`GCE_RUNTIME_SESSION_STATE_ARTIFACT_V1_CURRENT_2026-09-25`**\n\n---\n\n# Where Intent + Objective are already strong\n\n### Session Frame V3 header\n\nIt already has:\n\n```text\nRAW INTENT:\n<what Don is actually saying/requesting>\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n<the concrete outcome Don is trying to achieve>\n\nCONTEXT:\n<why this matters / surrounding constraint>\n```\n\nSo the interpretive layer is already there.\n\nThe rule is also exactly right:\n\n> Don Intent Snapshot is interpretive, not authoritative.  \n> If Don corrects it, update immediately.\n\nThat is important because tonight showed why.\n\n---\n\n# Executive Council header is even better\n\nIt currently has:\n\n```text\nRAW INTENT\nOBJECTIVE\nWHY / CONTEXT\nINTENT CONFIDENCE\n```\n\nThen separately:\n\n```text\nCURRENT QUESTION\nCURRENT POSITION\nKNOWN\nUNKNOWN\nCONFLICT\nASSUMPTIONS IN USE\nAUTHORITY BOUNDARY\n```\n\nAnd then a **drift baseline**:\n\n```text\nBASELINE INTENT\nCURRENT INTENT\nMATERIAL CHANGE SINCE BASELINE\nDRIFT STATUS\n```\n\nThat is already very close to what you’re describing.\n\n---\n\n# Shared Services header\n\nFor Luce/Falcon/Magpie/etc., it currently uses:\n\n```text\nDON / REQUESTER INTENT\nOBJECTIVE\nSCOPE\nOUT OF SCOPE\nACCEPTANCE CONDITION\nINTENT CONFIDENCE\n```\n\nThat’s excellent for bounded execution.\n\nIt answers:\n\n> What was I asked to do?  \n> What observable thing proves I’m done?\n\n---\n\n# The Footer is already doing the important close\n\nThis is the part you were remembering.\n\nThe **Executive Council Footer** explicitly contains:\n\n```text\nENTRY INTENT\nENTRY OBJECTIVE\n\nEXIT OBJECTIVE STATE:\nACHIEVED | PARTIAL | BLOCKED | CHANGED | SUPERSEDED\n\nCURRENT INTENT AT EXIT\nCURRENT OBJECTIVE AT EXIT\n\nINTENT / OBJECTIVE DELTA\nDRIFT STATUS\n```\n\nThat is exactly the mechanism that should have caught our issue tonight.\n\nIf:\n\n```text\nOBJECTIVE:\nDon can operate normally\n```\n\nand we proved:\n\n```text\nHYPOTHESIS 1:\nInternet is the problem\n\nRESULT:\nFALSE\n```\n\nwe are **not done**, because:\n\n```text\nEXIT OBJECTIVE STATE != ACHIEVED\n```\n\nThat’s your point.\n\n---\n\n# Runtime State Artifact\n\nThis is also already strong.\n\nIt requires every material state write to restate:\n\n```text\nINTENT\nOBJECTIVE\nCURRENT_TASK\nCURRENT_STATE\nACTIVE_TODO\nSCOPE\nNEXT_ACTION\nEXIT / STOP CONDITION\n```\n\nAnd importantly:\n\n> Intent and objective must be restated explicitly rather than inherited implicitly.\n\nThat’s already designed specifically for drift detection.\n\n---\n\n# What is missing\n\nThere is **no explicit first-class HYPOTHESIS lifecycle**.\n\nRight now hypotheses get buried inside:\n\n- `CURRENT QUESTION`\n- `ASSUMPTIONS IN USE`\n- `KNOWN / UNKNOWN`\n- active to-do items\n- investigative prose\n\nThat’s why a seat can accidentally behave as though disproving the user's proposed cause means the job is complete.\n\nWe need this distinction mechanically visible:\n\n```text\nOBJECTIVE\nWhat state are we trying to produce?\n\nINTENT\nWhy / what are we fundamentally trying to accomplish?\n\nHYPOTHESIS\nWhat explanation or route are we testing right now?\n```\n\nAnd then:\n\n```text\nHYPOTHESIS STATUS:\nUNTESTED | TESTING | SUPPORTED | REJECTED | INCONCLUSIVE\n\nEVIDENCE:\n<what proved/disproved it>\n\nOBJECTIVE IMPACT:\nACHIEVED | STILL OPEN | CHANGED\n```\n\nThat last field is the killer.\n\n---\n\n# Your operating loop\n\nWhat you just articulated tonight is:\n\n```text\nDON SIGNAL\n   ↓\nINTENT\n   ↓\nOBJECTIVE\n   ↓\nHYPOTHESIS 1\n   ↓\nTEST\n   ↓\nSUPPORTED / REJECTED\n   ↓\nOBJECTIVE ACHIEVED?\n   │\n   ├── YES → close\n   │\n   └── NO\n       ↓\n    HYPOTHESIS 2\n       ↓\n      TEST\n       ↓\n      ...\n```\n\nSo:\n\n> **A failed hypothesis closes the hypothesis, not the objective.**\n\nThat needs to be canon.\n\n---\n\n# Example from tonight\n\n```text\nINTENT:\nDetermine why Don cannot operate the machine normally.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\nRestore responsive terminals/browser/work environment.\n\nHYPOTHESIS 1:\nInternet connectivity is causing the degradation.\n\nRESULT:\nREJECTED.\n\nOBJECTIVE STATE:\nSTILL OPEN.\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```text\nHYPOTHESIS 2:\nPowerShell/startup architecture and profile-root runtime contamination\nare causing the degradation.\n\nRESULT:\nSUPPORTED.\n\nEVIDENCE:\nNeutralizing the startup hooks immediately restored normal operation.\n\nOBJECTIVE STATE:\nACHIEVED.\n```\n\nThat is **dramatically cleaner** than arguing about whether the original guess was correct.\n\n---\n\n## My recon conclusion\n\nThe current framework is already about **80–90% there**.\n\nWe do **not** need another session framework redesign.\n\nWe need one surgical addition across the existing family:\n\n**`HYPOTHESIS / TEST / RESULT / OBJECTIVE IMPACT`**\n\nMost importantly in:\n\n- Executive Council Header\n- Mid-Flight Frame\n- Checkpoint\n- Executive Council Footer\n- Shared Services where investigative work applies\n- Runtime Session State Artifact\n\nAnd the orchestrator/controller rule becomes:\n\n> **Never close because a hypothesis was resolved. Close only when the objective exit condition is satisfied or explicitly changed/blocked/superseded.**\n\nThat is the framework lesson from tonight.", "text_chars": 5723, "code_blocks": 17, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "3c5eb266-217e-4773-93da-62fc6a282c29", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790402270.0254068, "updated_at": 1790402444.059326, "statu